          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection"} connection
            the
            %em covariant derivative
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            is a measure for how that section fails to be constant with respect to the connection.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ForConnectionsOnInfinityBundles
            In the context of connections on
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We give here a definition of covariant derivatives that is natural in the general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            in that it applies to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} connections on ∞-bundles
          %p
            We start by describing this just for ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connections+on+a+bundle"} connections on a bundle
            and demonstrate how this general abstract definition reproduces the traditional definitions found in the literature.
          %p
            The central statement is: a covariant derivative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \sigma
            of a section may be identified with the 1-form
            = succeed "-component" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ∇
                  %mi σ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla \nabla \sigma = F_\nabla \sigma
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
            on its curvature 1-form.
          %h4#ActionLieAlgebroidCohomology Preliminaries on action Lie algebroid cohomology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : G \times V \to V
            a smooth
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V//G
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lie(V//G)
            corresponding to this is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
          %p
            Below we shall define covariant derivatives as curvature components of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebroid+valued+forms"} ∞-Lie algebroid valued forms
            with values in this action Lie algebroid. To prepare the ground for this, the following observation recalls some basic facts.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of the action Lie algebroid is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(Lie(V//G)) = (\wedge^\bullet_{C^\infty(V)} \mathfrak{g}^*, d_{\rho})
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the differential acts on functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C^\infty(V)
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi f
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_\rho : f \mapsto \rho(-)(-)^* f \in C^\infty(V)\otimes \mathfrak{g}^*
                  \\,.
          %p
            Explicitly, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in \mathfrak{g}
            this sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d_\rho f)(t)
            which is the derivative along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi e
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T_e G
            of the function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ρ
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times V \stackrel{\rho}{\to}V \stackrel{f}{\to} \mathbb{R}
          %p
            Even more explicitly, if we choose local coordinates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v^k\} : \mathbb{R}^{dim V} \to V
            on a patch, and choose a basis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t^a\}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            then we have that restricted to this patch the differential is on generators given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi f
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi μ
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi k
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_\rho : f \mapsto \rho^\mu{}_a t^a \wedge \partial_k f
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_\rho : t^a \mapsto - \frac{1}{2} C^a{}_{b c} t^b \wedge t^c
                  \\,.
          %p
            Specifically for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a finite dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : G
            a
            %em linear
            action,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v^k\}
            a choice of basis of that vector space and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f= f_k v^k
            , we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi k
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_k := \partial_k f) \in \mathbb{R}^{dim V}
            are the components vector of the dual vector given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in this basis, and the above gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
            form of the action
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi l
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi l
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_\rho : v^k \mapsto t^a \rho_a{}^k{}_l  v^l
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice for completeness that the equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d_\rho)^2 = 0
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            of the Lie bracket and the action property of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi ρ
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi b
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi l
                  %mo −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi l
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi l
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_\rho d_\rho v^k =
                  (t^a \wedge t^b \rho_a{}^k{}_r \rho_b{}^r{}_l
                  \-
                  \\frac{1}{2}C^a{}_{b c}t^b \wedge t^c \rho_a{}^k{}_l )
                  v^l
                  \\,.
          %p
            These local formulas shall be useful below for recognizing from our general abstract definition of covariant derivative the formulas traditionally given in the literature. For that notice that in the above local coordinates further restricting attention to linear actions, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            of the action Lie algebroid is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi dim
                          %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W(Lie(V//G)) = (\wedge^\bullet_{C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{dim V})} ( \Gamma(T^* \mathbb{R}^{dim V}) \oplus \mathfrak{g}^* \oplus \mathfrak{g}^*[1]), d_{W_\rho})
          %p where the differential is given on generators by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi l
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi l
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_{W_\rho} : v^k \mapsto \rho_a{}^k{}_l t^a \wedge v^l + d_{dR} v^k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
